 {
 id: 'mp3-quality',
 q: 'What audio quality does TikSaveHub provide?',
 a: 'TikSaveHub extracts audio at the highest bitrate available from the source video. Most TikTok videos carry 128kbps AAC audio, which converts to a clean MP3 file. The output matches what you hear on TikTok. No extra compression, no quality loss during conversion.\n\nOne thing to know: TikSaveHub can\'t improve audio that was already compressed by TikTok. If the source is 128kbps, the MP3 will be 128kbps. But it won\'t be worse. The conversion process is lossless. What goes in comes out, just in MP3 format instead of AAC.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-iphone',
 q: 'Can I convert TikTok videos to MP3 on my iPhone?',
 a: 'Works on any iPhone with Safari (iOS 13 or later). Open TikTok, copy the video link, switch to Safari, paste the link into TikSaveHub, and tap Download. The MP3 file lands in Safari\'s downloads manager. Pull down to see it, then tap the magnifying glass to open it in the Files app.\n\nOlder iPhones running iOS 12 or below sometimes block downloads entirely. If that happens, switching to Chrome on the same phone usually fixes it. The tool doesn\'t care which browser runs it. It\'s the OS that occasionally causes issues.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-devices',
 q: 'Does TikSaveHub work on Android and PC?',
 a: 'Any device with a modern browser. Android phones, Windows PCs, Macs, Linux machines, tablets. Doesn\'t matter. TikSaveHub is entirely browser-based, so there\'s nothing to install.',
