 {
 id: 'mp3-free',
 q: 'Is TikSaveHub free to use?',
 a: 'Completely free. No sign-up, no email collection, no hidden subscription tier. Paste a link, convert the audio, done.\n\nMost "free" TikTok audio converters start pushing a paid plan after five or six conversions. TikSaveHub doesn\'t. Unlimited conversions, zero cost. The processing runs server-side, so there\'s no browser extension to install and no app to download.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-account',
 q: 'Do I need a TikTok account?',
 a: 'No TikTok account needed. As long as the video is publicly accessible, TikSaveHub can extract the audio. Copy the link via Share → Copy Link, paste it into the tool, and the conversion starts. Private or restricted videos won\'t work. But TikSaveHub will tell you that honestly instead of showing a confusing error.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-legal',
 q: 'Is it legal to download TikTok audio?',
 a: 'Saving TikTok audio for personal use. Listening offline, keeping a favorite sound. Falls into a gray area that\'s broadly tolerated. TikTok\'s Terms of Service technically prohibit downloading outside the app, but that clause targets automated scraping and bulk redistribution, not someone saving one audio clip.\n\nCommercial use is different. Using TikTok audio in an ad, a YouTube video, a podcast, or any monetized content requires explicit permission from the original creator. Copyright applies to the audio itself, not just the video. Credit the creator, don\'t monetize their work without permission.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-speed',
 q: 'How long does the conversion take?',
 a: 'About two to three seconds on a standard broadband connection. The server fetches the TikTok video, strips the audio track, and converts it to MP3 in one pass. On slower mobile networks, it might take five seconds. The bottleneck is usually the file transfer, not the conversion itself.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-private',
 q: 'Can I convert private TikTok videos to MP3?',
 a: 'No. TikSaveHub only works with public videos. Private or friends-only content isn\'t accessible through TikTok\'s public API. No legitimate converter can bypass this. It\'s a hard technical wall, not a policy choice.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-format',
 q: 'What file format will I get?',
 a: 'MP3. That\'s the format. Works on every device, every music player, every operating system. The file extension is .mp3.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-limits',
 q: 'Are there any limits?',
 a: 'No daily caps, no conversion quotas, no premium ceiling. Convert as many TikTok videos as needed. Every conversion processes in roughly the same two-to-three-second window regardless of how many have already been done that day.',
 },
 {
 id: 'mp3-why',
 q: 'Why use TikSaveHub instead of other converters?',
 a: 'Honestly, most TikTok MP3 converters are frustrating to use. SSSTikTok buries downloads under three layers of pop-up ads. SnapTik has started gating conversions behind daily free limits. SaveFrom wants account creation before anything works. These aren\'t rumors. They\'re consistent patterns users report across forums and review sites.\n\nTikSaveHub takes a different approach: paste a link, get an MP3, done. No ads interrupting the flow, no account walls, no daily caps. The conversion runs server-side (faster than browser-based tools), and the output is a clean MP3 that plays everywhere. It\'s not complicated. It\'s just honest about what a converter should do.',
 },
];

const faqJsonLd = JSON.stringify({
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@type': 'FAQPage',
 mainEntity: faqData.map((faq) => ({
 '@type': 'Question',
 name: faq.q,
 acceptedAnswer: {
 '@type': 'Answer',
 text: faq.a.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ''),
 },
 })),
});
