 <h2 id="mp3-legal-headline" class="section-headline">
 Is it legal to download TikTok audio?
 </h2>
 </div>

 <div style="max-width:680px;width:100%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--spacing-lg);text-align:left;">
 <div style="padding:var(--spacing-xl);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);border:1px solid var(--color-hairline);background-color:var(--color-canvas);">
 <h3 style="font-size:var(--text-display-sm);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.6px;color:var(--color-ink);margin:0 0 var(--spacing-sm) 0;">Personal use is generally fine.</h3>
 <p style="font-size:var(--text-body-sm);color:var(--color-body);line-height:1.65;margin:0;">
 Saving TikTok audio for offline listening, keeping a favorite sound, or personal reference. That falls under personal use and is broadly tolerated. TikTok's Terms of Service technically prohibit downloading outside the app, but that clause targets automated bots scraping entire libraries, not a person saving one audio clip. The legal reality is more nuanced than the ToS text suggests.
 </p>
 </div>

 <div style="padding:var(--spacing-xl);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);border:1px solid var(--color-hairline);background-color:var(--color-canvas);">
 <h3 style="font-size:var(--text-display-sm);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.6px;color:var(--color-ink);margin:0 0 var(--spacing-sm) 0;">Commercial use requires permission.</h3>
 <p style="font-size:var(--text-body-sm);color:var(--color-body);line-height:1.65;margin:0;">
 Using TikTok audio in an ad, a YouTube compilation, a podcast, or any monetized content requires explicit permission from the original creator. Copyright applies to the audio itself, not just the video. Get written permission or risk a takedown.
 </p>
 </div>

 <div style="padding:var(--spacing-xl);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);border:1px solid var(--color-hairline);background-color:var(--color-canvas);">
 <h3 style="font-size:var(--text-display-sm);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.6px;color:var(--color-ink);margin:0 0 var(--spacing-sm) 0;">Credit the creator.</h3>
 <p style="font-size:var(--text-body-sm);color:var(--color-body);line-height:1.65;margin:0;">
 Even for personal sharing, crediting the original creator is the right thing to do. Tag the creator, mention their username, link back to the original. Takes five seconds and gives credit where it's due.
 </p>
 </div>

 <p style="font-size:var(--text-body-sm);color:var(--color-body);line-height:1.65;margin:var(--spacing-md) 0 0 0;font-style:italic;">
 This article is for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal advice. Consult a qualified lawyer for your specific situation.
 </p>

 <p style="font-size:var(--text-body-sm);color:var(--color-body);line-height:1.65;margin:0;">
